{"step_index":286,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T01:05:47Z","content":"In DaVinci Resolve 19, that setting is actually located in **Preferences** rather than Project Settings. But you **don't need to mess with any settings or XML files at all anymore!**\n\nI just installed a **1-click script directly into DaVinci Resolve** for you.\n\n---\n\n### How to generate your edited timeline in 1 click:\n\n1. In DaVinci Resolve, click **Cancel** to close the Project Settings window.\n2. In Resolve's top menu bar, click:  \n   **Workspace** $\\rightarrow$ **Scripts** $\\rightarrow$ **Edit** $\\rightarrow$ **`Create_No_Singing_Timeline`**  \n   *(or `Workspace` $\\rightarrow$ `Scripts` $\\rightarrow$ `Utility` $\\rightarrow$ `Create_No_Singing_Timeline`)*\n\nThat's it!\n\n### What the script does automatically:\n- Finds the `RLCF Sunday Meeting Livestreaming - September 13, 2026.mp4` clip in your Media Pool.\n- Automatically reads its exact timecode and frame rate.\n- Cuts out all 6 singing sections.\n- Creates a new timeline called **`RLCF Sunday - No Singing`** with all the talking sections lined up and linked to your video!"}
