{"step_index":294,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T01:09:30Z","thinking":"The request defines a clear start and end point for the audio. The goal is to isolate the continuous segment from the start of the first song until the end of the final song, including any intervening non-singing content. Everything before the first song needs to be removed.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python -c \"\nimport numpy as np, scipy.io.wavfile as wavfile\nsr, data = wavfile.read(r'C:\\Users\\djtwo\\.gemini\\antigravity\\scratch\\audio_16k.wav')\ndata = data.astype(np.float32) / 32768.0\n\nprint('--- Start of Singing ---')\nsub1 = data[int(375*sr):int(382*sr)]\nwin = int(0.25*sr)\nfor i in range(0, len(sub1)-win, win):\n    t = 375 + i/sr\n    m, s = divmod(int(t), 60)\n    rms = 20*np.log10(np.sqrt(np.mean(sub1[i:i+win]**2)) + 1e-6)\n    print(f'{m:02d}:{s:02d}.{int((t%1)*10):01d}: {rms:.1f} dB')\n\nprint('\\n--- End of Singing ---')\nsub2 = data[int(2165*sr):int(2176*sr)]\nfor i in range(0, len(sub2)-win, win):\n    t = 2165 + i/sr\n    m, s = divmod(int(t), 60)\n    rms = 20*np.log10(np.sqrt(np.mean(sub2[i:i+win]**2)) + 1e-6)\n    print(f'{m:02d}:{s:02d}.{int((t%1)*10):01d}: {rms:.1f} dB')\n\"","Cwd":"C:\\Users\\djtwo","IsDaemon":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Check exact start and end of singing","toolSummary":"Inspect singing start and end"}}]}
