{"step_index":306,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T01:23:50Z","thinking":"The request implies a timeline divided into distinct segments, each representing a single song, including the speaking sections between the songs. This suggests either slicing the timeline into labeled clips or creating individual sections for each song and the speech. The core task is to create a visual representation that separates the distinct audio elements into individual parts.\n\n\nConsidered three options for representing the audio: individual clips per song/speaking section, timeline markers on each song, or a combination of both with cuts and labeled, color-coded markers. Focused on the most effective method for an editor to manipulate individual sections.\n\nDecided to prioritize the combination of timeline cuts at song boundaries with named, color-coded markers for each song's start. This ensures both clear visual segmentation and easy navigation. Confirmed understanding of the required output structure.\n\n\n","tool_calls":[{"name":"run_command","args":{"CommandLine":"python -c \"\nwith open(r'C:\\ProgramData\\Blackmagic Design\\DaVinci Resolve\\Support\\Developer\\Scripting\\README.txt', 'r', encoding='utf-8', errors='ignore') as f:\n    lines = f.readlines()\n\nfor i, line in enumerate(lines):\n    if 'AddMarker(' in line:\n        for j in range(max(0, i-2), min(len(lines), i+8)):\n            print(lines[j].strip())\n        print('='*40)\n\"","Cwd":"C:\\Users\\djtwo","IsDaemon":false,"WaitMsBeforeAsync":5000,"toolAction":"Check AddMarker syntax in Resolve API docs","toolSummary":"Check AddMarker API"}}]}
