{"step_index":317,"source":"MODEL","type":"PLANNER_RESPONSE","status":"DONE","created_at":"2026-09-16T01:40:34Z","content":"Yes, absolutely! For YouTube, you need two things:\n\n1. **The YouTube Chapters Text** (to paste directly into your YouTube video description so YouTube creates clickable chapter markers on the scrubber bar).\n2. **The DaVinci Resolve Timeline & Export Settings** (to get maximum video and audio quality on YouTube).\n\n---\n\n### 1. Ready-to-Paste YouTube Video Chapters\nCopy and paste this directly into your **YouTube Video Description**:\n\n```text\n00:00 Song 1: Come Be Enthroned On Our Praise\n02:29 Sharing: Power of Christ Risen\n03:05 Song 2: See What A Morning (Christ Is Risen)\n06:22 Prayer & Intercession\n17:33 Song 3: Jesus I Sing / Hymn\n21:27 Sharing: Life of Christ\n21:50 Song 4: All To His Time\n23:41 Sharing: Christ In Saints\n23:52 Song 5: O To Tongues of Fire\n26:02 Sharing: Forgiveness & The Pit\n27:04 Song 6: Worship Closing Song\n```\n\n> **Why this works:** YouTube requires chapters to start at `00:00` and have at least 3 timestamps. When you paste this into your description, YouTube will automatically chop the video player into interactive sections with these song titles.\n\n---\n\n### 2. Best YouTube Export Settings in DaVinci Resolve\n\nWhen you are ready to export on Resolve's **Deliver** page (the rocket icon at the bottom):\n\n1. **Select the YouTube Preset** (top-left of the Deliver page) or **Custom Export**.\n2. **Resolution**: Set to **`2560 x 1440` (1440p)** or **`3840 x 2160` (4K)**:\n   - *Pro Tip:* Even though your source is 720p, exporting at 1440p/4K forces YouTube to process your video with its premium **VP9 / AV01 codec** at a much higher bitrate, so it won't look blurry or pixelated on YouTube!\n3. **Embed Chapter Markers (Automatic)**:\n   - In the Deliver settings under the **Video** tab, scroll down to **Chapters**.\n   - Check **Chapters from markers** and select **Cyan** (the color our script used).\n   - Resolve will embed the song chapters directly into the MP4 file metadata!\n4. **Audio**:\n   - Format: **AAC**\n   - Data Rate: **320 Kb/s**\n   - Sample Rate: **48000 Hz**\n\n---\n\n### Are you also looking to make vertical \"YouTube Shorts\" (9:16)?\nIf you want to pull out individual songs or short clips to post as vertical **YouTube Shorts / Reels**, let me know and I can create a vertical 1080x1920 timeline preset for you!","thinking":"Considering \"make timeline for youtube,\" the most likely interpretation is creating YouTube chapter timestamps. This involves generating a formatted list of timestamps suitable for a video description, enabling interactive chapters within the YouTube player.\n\n\nMultiple interpretations exist, including timeline optimization, vertical video, or chapter creation. Chapter list generation is a primary focus, considering that YouTube requires specific formatting and minimum chapter counts starting at 00:00. This also involves examining the timeline and calculating chapter timestamps relative to the video's start.\n\n\n- The video chapters are extracted and formatted for direct pasting into the YouTube description box. This provides the user the chaptered list:\n        - `0:00` - Song 1: Title\n        - `0:33` - Song 3: Jesus I Sing / Hymn\n        - `21:27` - Sharing: Life of Christ\n        - `21:50` - Song 4: All To His Time\n        - `23:41` - Sharing: Christ In Saints\n        - `23:52` - Song 5: O To Tongues of Fire\n        - `26:02` - Sharing: Forgiveness & The Pit\n        - `27:04` - Song 6: Worship Closing Song\n- To ensure optimal YouTube encoding, the timeline resolution should be set to 1440p or 4K.  Chapter markers can be embedded during export using Resolve's Deliver page by selecting Cyan markers.\n- Considering potential use, it is noted a separate vertical 9:16 Shorts timeline could be readily created for individual songs.\n\n\n"}
